  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fedex Supply Chain Distribution System has $100M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Fedex Supply Chain Distribution System received 13 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $7.7M. Obligations fell 75.5% year over year. Historical obligations show a multi-year rise from $253M in FY22 to $409M in FY26, followed by the current-year total of $100M for FY27. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $100M of obligations in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice recorded $15K in obligations during the same period. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity, while award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
